(Baldwin Insurance Group faces pre-closing friction arising from its Up-C dual-class structure, insider rollover equity, and lack of a majority-of-the-minority voting) Tj
T* (condition. The transaction relies solely on a single-class vote of Class A and Class B shares. Insiders commit ~30% of total voting power \(~15.0% beneficial) Tj
T* (ownership\) and secure a ~7.3% rollover into Topco common equity alongside institutional sponsors \(DFO and Sequence\), while unaffiliated Class A stockholders are) Tj
T* (cashed out at $32.50 per share. Concurrently, TRA Amendment No. 1 directs up to $298,450,598 in accelerated cash termination payments exclusively to TRA) Tj
T* (unitholders, excluding public stockholders. Without a non-waivable majority-of-the-minority voting condition, the buyout fails the MFW dual-cleansing standard under) Tj
T* (Delaware law, exposing the transaction to entire fairness scrutiny and potential fiduciary breach litigation.) Tj
